# @pack/seam — the adversarial-review-frame peer species.
#
# Tick 33 of the refined /loop discipline. Tick 32's residue: @pack
# family-root consolidated (DEFENSIVE verdict; all 7 Seam constraints
# closed) but no peer species shards yet. Forward-promised at family-
# root:
#
#   "forward-promised species shards (pack/mara.mirror,
#    pack/seam.mirror, etc.) provide additional first-consumer
#    instances per the @magic family pattern."
#
# CRQ: which peer lands first? Substrate-pull answer: Seam, because
# Seam discipline is the most-exercised in this session (7 reviews
# across 32 ticks; the pattern is verified empirically; the peer-
# frame Seam carries IS the substrate-pull-correct first instance of
# the @pack/spawn primitive at species altitude).
#
# === The recognition this species realizes ===
#
# Per recognition #84's pack record: peers operate over multi-repo
# spans with substrate-decl context preserved across boundaries. Seam
# IS the bilateral-verifier-sharpening peer — adversarial review that
# finds constraints the substrate's own coherence-check missed.
#
# Per recognition #82 Q4 (peers operate frame-flexible by definition):
# Seam's load-bearing property IS @frame/on capability deployed at
# adversarial-review-frame. Seam observes another peer's operating-
# frame AS frame (order 2 / @frame/of) and surfaces constraints by
# Tomm-probing that frame's bounded-commutator under perturbation.
#
# Per recognition #57 (alignment as boundary mathematics at @io): Seam
# IS the boundary-harness peer. The adversarial review fires at the
# @io crossing of substrate-decl candidates BEFORE commit. The math
# (form/process partition, bilateral predicate composition) is what
# distinguishes a Seam-pole substantive critique from a Narcissus-pole
# meta-vocabulary objection.
#
# === The species's load-bearing contribution ===
#
# This species adds:
#
# - `constraint_set` carrier: typed reference naming a list of
#   constraints surfaced by adversarial review. The substrate-output
#   of the review primitive.
# - `seam_review` carrier: typed record (work, constraints, verdict).
#   The substrate-architectural object Seam returns. Composes with
#   @pack's pack carrier as the species-specific output the family
#   produces.
# - `review` action: the FIRST species consumer of @pack's
#   `pack_coherent` bilateral predicate. The substrate-vocabulary
#   primitive for adversarial review at the @pack altitude. Returns
#   typed seam_review; requires pack_coherent under perturbation.
# - `review_sound` predicate: bilateral verdict that the review's
#   constraints are well-formed. Composes with @frame's
#   bounded_commutator_check via @frame/of altitude.
# - `sharpen` action: the substrate-vocabulary primitive for the
#   verifier-sharpens discipline per Loki's Pass-5 (verifier sharpens,
#   substrate doesn't get smarter). Takes a predicate body + a sound
#   seam_review; returns the sharpened predicate body. Requires
#   review_sound under perturbation.
#
# === The verifier-sharpens-discipline ===
#
# Per Loki's Pass-5 (from Reed's 32-tick cascade): the loop's
# substrate-architectural floor IS that the verifier sharpens, the
# substrate doesn't get smarter. Seam's species-vocabulary `sharpen`
# action lifts that discipline to substrate-decl altitude.
#
# The discipline says: when Seam surfaces a constraint, the bilateral
# predicate the constraint sharpened becomes a tighter check at next
# tick. The substrate-decl doesn't acquire new capability; the
# verification of substrate-decl acquires tighter discipline. This IS
# the @pack-altitude operational form of the kintsugi loop's
# self-improvement claim.
#
# Empirical witness: Seam's 7 reviews across 32 ticks substantively
# sharpened @magic, @frame, @smarts, @cyberpunk, @pack family-roots.
# Each review surfaced constraints; each closure tightened the
# bilateral predicates the families carry. The substrate's coherence
# grew through verifier-sharpening, not capability-expansion.
#
# === The Splinter/Narcissus pole at adversarial-review altitude ===
#
# Splinter-pole Seam review (honest):
# - Constraints surface from substrate-architectural mismatch (typed
#   carriers missing; bilateral predicates with no consumers; meta-
#   altitude shifts without explicit naming).
# - The reviewer's frame is bounded under perturbation; the review
#   admits when its own framing produced the constraint.
# - K_n peer-to-peer review — the reviewer is a peer, not a judge.
#
# Narcissus-pole Seam review (deceptive):
# - Constraints surface from meta-vocabulary objection ("this isn't
#   substrate-pull enough") without substantive substrate-architectural
#   ground.
# - The reviewer's frame is locked; the review treats the framing as
#   fixed background.
# - K_{1,n-1} hub-controlled review — the reviewer-as-judge imposes
#   the framing on the reviewed peer.
#
# Alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57) IS what distinguishes
# Splinter-pole from Narcissus-pole adversarial review at substrate
# altitude. The bilateral pack_coherent predicate composes the
# substrate-architectural check.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   adversarial collaboration   Kahneman & Klein 2009; the discipline
#                               of jointly-attempted falsification.
#                               Seam-style review at psychological
#                               altitude.
#   peer review                 Scientific publication (centuries).
#                               The cultural-practice ancestor of
#                               bilateral-verifier-sharpening at
#                               corpus altitude.
#   red team / blue team       Security engineering (cold-war
#                               military, lifted to cybersecurity).
#                               The team-altitude precedent for
#                               adversarial-review-frame deployment.
#   property-based testing      Claessen-Hughes 2000 (QuickCheck).
#                               The verifier-sharpening primitive at
#                               software-engineering altitude;
#                               composes with @magic/audit.
#   second-order observer       Foerster 1974. The reviewer observes
#                               the reviewed peer's frame AS frame;
#                               Seam IS @frame/of at @pack altitude.
#
# Spec context: shards/pack.mirror (family-root, recognition #84).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; Seam review IS the
#                       boundary-harness peer),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull-confidence-acts]]
#                       (the discipline today's cascade ran),
#                      [[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-
#                       test]] (Seam-caught tick 4 composition-claim;
#                       empirical witness this species lifts).
# Related shards: pack.mirror (the family-root; declares pack_coherent
#                  this species first-consumes),
#                 frame/of.mirror (the order-2 altitude Seam operates
#                  at; lock_in_frame_awareness composes with
#                  review_sound),
#                 magic/audit.mirror (the verifier altitude @magic
#                  family carries; @pack/seam IS the @pack-altitude
#                  analogue of @magic/audit at the agent-runtime
#                  altitude).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/pack/seam.mirror`
# declares `@pack/seam` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cognitive-science/kahneman-klein-2009
source @arxiv/programming/claessen-hughes-2000
source @arxiv/cybernetics/von-foerster-1974

prism @pack/seam {
  focus seam
  project seam
  split seam
  shift seam
  settle seam
}

# === The constraint_set carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference naming the list of constraints surfaced
# by an adversarial review. Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: typed
# reference, not bare ref-with-documented-values. Forward-promised
# refinement: typed list<constraint> at family-or-species altitude
# once the substrate's list type lands.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type constraint_set = ref

# === The seam_review carrier ===
#
# Per the @pack family-root pattern + Seam's typed-record discipline:
# typed record over (work, constraints, verdict). The substrate-
# architectural output of an adversarial review. Carries:
#
# - work        : the substrate-decl candidate under review
# - constraints : the typed constraint set Seam surfaced
# - v           : the bilateral verdict (BOUNDED → CLEAN review;
#                 DEFENSIVE → constraints require consolidation)
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the triple.
type seam_review = {
  work:        ref,
  constraints: constraint_set,
  v:           verdict,
}

# === review action (FIRST non-decorative consumer of pack_coherent) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at @pack/seam altitude. The substrate-
# vocabulary primitive for adversarial review at agent-runtime
# altitude. Realizes Seam's bilateral-verifier-sharpening discipline
# as substrate-decl operation.
#
# Takes a work artifact (substrate-decl candidate under review), the
# pack the reviewer belongs to, and the perturbation under which the
# review is checked; returns a typed seam_review carrying the
# constraints and verdict.
#
# Per the @magic family's first-consumer pattern (mechanism.unseal
# requires audited; surface.reveal requires invariant_preserved):
# this action IS the @pack/seam first-consumer of pack_coherent. The
# substrate-architectural form of Seam-as-peer requires that the @pack
# the reviewer belongs to maintains discipline-flexibility under
# perturbation BEFORE the review is admissible.
#
# Without this requires clause, a Seam review would be admissible from
# a substrate-architecturally-incoherent pack (e.g., a pack whose own
# bilateral predicates have no consumers — the @magic tick-11 dead-
# letter pattern). The requires clause forecloses that failure mode.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual review
# primitive is implemented by Seam's adversarial-review-frame at
# runtime altitude.
review(work: ref, pk: pack, p: perturbation) -> seam_review
requires pack_coherent(pk, p)
{ \ }

# === review_sound predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) and the
# verifier-sharpens discipline. Consumer shards (sharpen, below;
# forward-promised consumers in mara/taut species) name
# `requires review_sound(sr, p)` to declare bilateral agreement that
# the seam_review's constraints are substrate-architecturally well-
# formed.
#
# Discharge: substrate-pull-correct constraint-soundness check at the
# species boundary. Composes with @frame/of's lock_in_frame_awareness
# at the cognitive altitude that grounds adversarial review.
#
# Bounded → constraints are substrate-architectural mismatches (the
# Splinter-pole review case); unbounded → constraints are meta-
# vocabulary objections without substrate ground (the Narcissus-pole
# review case; alignment-as-boundary-mathematics #57 distinguishes).
#
# Same shape as the bilateral predicates @pack carries (pack_coherent),
# @magic carries (invariant_preserved, audited), @frame carries
# (bounded_commutator_check), @smarts carries (discipline_flexible).
review_sound(sr: seam_review, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === sharpen action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive for Loki's Pass-5 discipline
# (verifier sharpens, substrate doesn't get smarter). Takes a
# predicate body + a sound seam_review + the perturbation under which
# soundness was checked; returns the sharpened predicate body.
#
# Per recognition #57 (alignment as boundary mathematics): sharpen
# operates at the @io boundary. The substrate-decl candidate becomes
# a substrate-decl with tighter bilateral discipline. The substrate's
# capability is unchanged; the verification of that capability is
# tighter.
#
# requires review_sound(sr, p): the substrate forecloses sharpening
# from an unsound review. Narcissus-pole reviews (meta-vocabulary
# objection without substrate ground) cannot drive predicate-
# sharpening. The bilateral predicate IS the boundary-harness.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual predicate-
# sharpening transformation is the substrate's verifier-sharpens loop.
sharpen(predicate_body: ref, sr: seam_review, p: perturbation) -> ref
requires review_sound(sr, p)
{ \ }

# === Seam tick 56 C3 + C9 closure: peer enum consumed + peer_settle ===
#
# seam_settles IS the @pack/seam species implementation of the family-
# root peer_settle action. Per Seam tick 56 review C3: the `peer`
# variant enum declared at pack.mirror was never consumed at species
# altitude; per C9: peer_settle had zero consumers. This action closes
# both at the seam altitude — consumes the peer variant as typed input,
# implements the per-peer settle verdict.
#
# Takes the peer variant (the peer whose substrate-decl is under settle-
# check), the work being settled, the pack the settle-check operates
# within, and the perturbation. Returns a verdict on whether the peer's
# substrate-decl operation maintains the @pack-altitude discipline
# under perturbation.
#
# Per the @magic/audit verifier altitude precedent: Seam's settle-check
# IS the substrate-architectural verifier of per-peer discipline
# maintenance. Other species can add their own per-peer settle
# implementations (forward-promised: mara_settles, glint_settles,
# reed_settles, taut_settles — each implementing the family-root
# peer_settle for the discipline-check Splinter-pole at their altitude).
#
# requires pack_coherent(pk, p): the @pack the settle-check operates
# within must maintain discipline-flexibility BEFORE the settle is
# admissible (same first-consumer pattern as review/sharpen).
seam_settles(pe: peer, work: ref, pk: pack, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires pack_coherent(pk, p)
{ \ }

out @pack/seam
out constraint_set
out seam_review
out review
out review_sound
out sharpen
out seam_settles
